<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Improving Planner with Generated Videos</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct experiments to evaluate the effectiveness of our generated data to fine-tune the planner. We compare two fine-tuning approaches: one is simply fine-tuning the planner on real-videos with 40K steps, and the other is to fine-tune on one million synthetic videos for 20K steps and then on real videos for 20K steps. The synthetic videos are generated with the same conditions as the real ones and the ground truth future trajectories are the same.
We evaluate the planner’s performance on real-world data to demonstrate the effectiveness of synthetic data in improving real-world performance. Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table V ‣ IV-C Improving Planner with Generated Videos ‣ IV Experiments ‣ Drive&amp;Gen: Co-Evaluating End-to-End Driving and Video Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a> presents the ADE of the different models. While fine-tuning solely on real data yields limited performance improvements, incorporating synthetic data from our generator effectively reduces the ADE at 5 seconds from 0.7548 to 0.7333. This demonstrates the potential of generating synthetic videos to enhance the performance of end-to-end planners.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table V</span>: </span><span id="S4.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ADE scores on real-world validation data, fine-tuned on different data mixtures. Here, “gen” refers to videos generated by our model.</span></figcaption>
